) values (
  1, $q$Qamar Abbas$q$, $q$قمر عباس$q$, $q$Visual artist & art educator$q$, $q$Lahore, Pakistan$q$, $q$Oshikhandass valley, Gilgit-Baltistan$q$, $q$1997$q$,
  $q$qartstudio3@gmail.com$q$, $q$abbas.khushall@gmail.com$q$, $q$+92 348 4653180$q$, array[$q$Q Art studio$q$, $q$E-130-A2, Gilani Street$q$, $q$Nadirbad$q$]::text[], array[$q$Anokha studio$q$, $q$Punjab Small Industries$q$, $q$Lahore$q$]::text[],
  $q$[{"label":"Instagram","handle":"@qamarabbas_artist","href":"https://www.instagram.com/qamarabbas_artist"},{"label":"Facebook","handle":"Qamar Abbas","href":"https://www.facebook.com/share/1BaZumZigu/"},{"label":"X","handle":"@KhushallArt","href":"https://x.com/KhushallArt"},{"label":"LinkedIn","handle":"Qamar Abbas","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/abbas-qamar-36126120b"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$https://3b787863-b885-47e2-9503-0d9532eb5825.filesusr.com/ugd/4e6f30_6491b999d50e4fc2a0f626c433eda06c.pdf$q$,
  $q$My name is Qamar Abbas, a Visual Artist born in 1997 in the Oshikhandass valley of Gilgit Baltistan. I graduated from the National College of Arts (NCA), Lahore, in 2020 with a degree in Fine Arts, specializing in painting.$q$, array[$q$My artistic journey reached a significant peak in 2025, where I participated in the Portrait of Quaid-e-Azam competition and group exhibition at Alhamra Art Council, the “Eid al-Etihad” group exhibition for the UAE National Day at Sambara Art Gallery, Karachi, and the Anamolka Award Exhibition at Punjab University Gallery. These followed a productive 2024, during which I showcased my work at the Artiade – Olympic of Art in New York and the “LIMINAL” group show at Haam Gallery, Lahore.$q$, $q$Earlier in my career, I was honored to win the Asia Pacific Regional Art Contest (Ozone2climate Change) in 2022 and was recognized as a top 10 winner at the 16th Young Artist Exhibition at Alhamra Art Council in 2019. My exhibition history also includes the Young Artists Exhibitions at the Hyderabad Arts Council in 2016 and the Karachi Arts Council in 2014. Beyond my studio practice, I am deeply committed to art education; during the COVID-19 pandemic, I organized workshops in my hometown schools to inspire young minds through visual expression.$q$]::text[], array[$q$Paper Birch (Bhojpatra) bark serves as my preferred work surface, which I incorporate into my ongoing “Echoes on Birch” series. Within this medium, I employ traditional scripts and calligraphic mark-making — particularly Khat-e-Suls — as vital visual elements to explore complex themes of landscape and cultural memory.$q$, $q$In parallel, my practice delves into conceptual investigations that subvert constitutional texts and currency-based imagery to critique systemic structures, hierarchies, and the visual representation of power.$q$]::text[], $q$I completed an art residency in Hunza, and I have contributed to art education as an art educator at Learning Alliance, Lahore.$q$, $q$Teaching is part of my practice. During the COVID-19 pandemic I organized workshops in my hometown schools to inspire young minds through visual expression, and I have served as an art educator at Learning Alliance, Lahore.$q$,
  $q$[{"title":"Line first","text":"Every lesson begins with control of the line — the root of drawing and of writing."},{"title":"Know the masters","text":"Students study the artists and traditions behind each style before making their own."},{"title":"Patience as practice","text":"Repetition is not boring; it is how the hand learns what the eye already sees."}]$q$::jsonb,
  $q$[{"title":"Share your idea","text":"The text or verse, the script you love, size, colours and where it will hang."},{"title":"Proposal & sketch","text":"I reply by email with a price, timeline and a first composition sketch."},{"title":"Creation","text":"The piece is written and finished by hand in the studio, with progress updates."},{"title":"Delivery","text":"Carefully packed and shipped within Pakistan or internationally."}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Verses, names, prayers or poetry — composed and written by hand, in a classical script or a contemporary style.$q$,
  array[$q$Buy an artwork$q$, $q$Commission a piece$q$, $q$Talk, class or collaboration$q$, $q$Something else$q$]::text[], '/media/hero-bark.webp', $q$Calligraphy on paper birch. Landscape, cultural memory, and the visual language of power.$q$, $q$Bhojpatra bark from the mountains of Gilgit-Baltistan, written on in Khat-e-Suls: landscape and cultural memory, one sheet at a time.$q$, $q$[{"k":"Education","v":"Fine Arts, painting: National College of Arts, Lahore (2020)"},{"k":"Recognition","v":"Winner, Asia Pacific Regional Art Contest (2022)"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To buy a work, commission a piece, or invite me for a talk or class — send a message and I’ll reply by email.$q$, $q$Qamar Abbas is a visual artist born in 1997 in the Oshikhandass valley of Gilgit-Baltistan, based in Lahore. Birch bark and ink, constitution and currency, charcoal portraits of the mountain people, and embroidery.$q$,
  '/media/portrait.jpg', $q$data:image/webp;base64,UklGRooAAABXRUJQVlA4IH4AAAAwBACdASoQABQAPwFqrE6rJiQiMAgBYCAJaQAD5RHF6NpgyAdjorLvxoAA/vK0k8vva/wzbuwYRgtiBB381G5ttonXWiSfWolM9Z4QFpEJi0u+rR8ZHIHeVZD7DILkPIPyrBOba10IqCiEJRaPJeF5owb72e2yqKZ/eBQAAAA=$q$
) on conflict (id) do nothing;



